HeySig speech-masking head, development build, November 9, 2026.
This is an experimental speech/background masking classifier, not a clinical
intelligibility measurement, speaker identity model or compatibility certification.

The existing YAMNet encoder remains unchanged, under its existing Apache-2.0
notice in environment/. A separately fitted 3-class linear head uses pooled
encoder features plus envelope modulation, pitch periodicity and zero crossings.
The original head is retained as masking-baseline.txt. A second head adds six
shared Kotlin spectral noise-suppression features. Both must agree before the
existing repeated-check policy can switch programs. No cleaned audio is played.
No separate inference runtime, speech recognition or network model is added.

Fitting sources: LibriSpeech (c) 2014 Vassil Panayotov, CC BY 4.0,
https://www.openslr.org/12/ . Prepared by V. Panayotov, G. Chen, D. Povey and
S. Khudanpur from LibriVox audiobooks. Development readers: zinniz (2277),
