Transforms: decode/resample mono 16kHz, bounded three-second windows; normalized
foreground/background mixes at +15/+3/-8dB SNR, matched -30/-45dBFS overall RMS;
digital low-pass/echo position proxies; short background excerpts may be tiled.
No foreground speech is tiled. No source recordings or transcripts are packaged
in the application. Only fixed model weights, source credits and licenses ship.
Heldout sources in sources.json are evaluation credits, not coefficient fitting.
Model training and independent-field acceptance are different; no qualification
is implied by packaging these weights. No source author endorses HeySig.

November 10, 2026: the HSGMASK2 spectral-suppression head is retired from
the phone package. Historical training provenance above is retained. The active
phone path combines masking-baseline.txt (HSGMASK1) with the neural denoiser
and fixed bands credited in separation/NOTICE. No wearer training is required.
